> I probably missed this in earlier conversation and I probably just have a
> wrong mental image of how this thing works but...
>
> We have some spinning tube things that people can go between.  How exactly
> does that work.  Is there a bridge like connection or when we talk of going
> between tubes are we talking about a shuttle type system?

It's a bridge-like connection. The two tubes are spinning in opposite 
directions and held some distance apart so that they orbit as one object. 
Corrections of some sort can be made by varying the two speeds slightly.

